llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: X86FixupSetCC is not run (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a zero-extended setcc. The pass
X86FixupSetCC, new in LLVM 3.9 (lib/Target/X86/X86FixupSetCC.cpp, added
to the pipeline in X86PassConfig::addPreRegAlloc), rewrites `setcc r8;
movzx r32, r8` as `xor r32, r32; ...; setcc r8` with the zeroing hoisted
before the flag-setting instruction. The game region was built without
it: 1,548 `setcc; movzx` pairs in 775 functions, and the 76 xor-before-
setcc hits are ordinary zeroed registers (round 113A, 0x30d620 and
0x2a58b7 checked); the library region has 234 pairs in 90 functions and
no xor form. With this patch 0x135e290, 0x135e2a0, 0x135e2d0, 0x135e330
and 0x135e460 compile to the base's bytes.

--- a/lib/Target/X86/X86TargetMachine.cpp
+++ b/lib/Target/X86/X86TargetMachine.cpp
@@ -375,7 +375,8 @@
 
 void X86PassConfig::addPreRegAlloc() {
   if (getOptLevel() != CodeGenOpt::None) {
-    addPass(createX86FixupSetCC());
+    // PS4: no X86FixupSetCC (new in LLVM 3.9): a zero-extended setcc stays
+    // `setcc; movzx`, as the earlier releases left it.
     addPass(createX86OptimizeLEAs());
     addPass(createX86CallFrameOptimization());
   }
